[statement]
With every installed package removed, apk removes `feed`, which needs
`lua` and `lua-expat`, before `lua5.4-expat`, which is installed for its
condition on `lua5.4` and `lua-expat`, needed by nothing, and listed
first: `lua5.4`, first in the database, pulls the removals waiting on it,
those through a name it provides at no version (`feed`, through `lua`)
before those through a condition (`lua5.4-expat`); `lua5.4-expat` frees
the names its condition states, last stated first. Reduced from a layered request
over Alpine v3.24 (`lua-feedparser`'s closure from v3.23 installed,
`gvpe-openrc` asked), its root made consistent by hand.

[repository]
P:x
V:1-r0

[installed]
P:lua5.4
V:5.4-r0
p:lua

P:lua-expat
V:1-r0

P:lua5.4-expat
V:1-r0
i:lua5.4 lua-expat

P:feed
V:1-r0
D:lua lua-expat

[request]
x

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove feed 1-r0
remove lua5.4-expat 1-r0
remove lua-expat 1-r0
remove lua5.4 5.4-r0
install x 1-r0
